"Whenever a six-year-old persistently asks 'Why?', they are essentially practicing the fundamentals of philosophical inquiry. Unfortunately, traditional elementary schooling frequently dampens this instinct by rewarding children for quickly reciting the single 'correct' answer rather than exploring how conclusions are reached. If primary teachers were instead trained to encourage open-ended questioning, evidence evaluation, and respectful disagreement, pupils would internalize healthy skepticism early on.",
