"Consequently, continuing education—often referred to as lifelong learning—has transitioned from an optional career booster into an absolute necessity for professional survival. Whether through evening university seminars, employer-sponsored workshops, or accredited online micro-credentials, workers must continuously upskill and reskill to remain employable. Beyond safeguarding against redundancy, lifelong learning stimulates cognitive vitality and empowers adults to pivot into entirely new sectors mid-career.",
