      "Henrik nodded reluctantly, conceding her point. 'You're right that individual precautions alone—like using VPNs—are insufficient against systemic tracking. Unless governments enforce strict data-minimization laws and penalize invasive tracking practices, true digital privacy will remain accessible only to tech-savvy elites.'"
