"First, intensive monoculture farming—growing a single genetic crop variety across vast expanses—severely degrades soil health and eliminates natural resilience. Continuous chemical tilling depletes organic matter, triggers widespread topsoil erosion, and reduces the soil's capacity to retain moisture during droughts. Furthermore, genetic uniformity leaves entire harvests dangerously vulnerable to novel pests and plant diseases, as witnessed during historical agricultural blights.",
