"Aerobic exercise stimulates the release of brain-derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF), a protein that promotes the growth of new neurons and strengthens synaptic connections critical for memory and executive function. Schools that have integrated daily physical activity into their schedules consistently report higher student concentration, improved classroom behavior, and stronger academic achievement—particularly in mathematics and reading.",
"Beyond cognitive enhancement, school sports cultivate vital social and emotional competencies. Participating in team athletics teaches adolescents resilience in the face of defeat, disciplined goal-setting, leadership, and constructive cooperation across diverse backgrounds. Moreover, establishing active habits during childhood combats rising rates of youth obesity and anxiety.",
