"Human dignity rests on the fundamental principle that every person possesses intrinsic worth and must never be treated merely as a biological specimen, a data point, or a commercial commodity. When tech corporations seek to monetize neural data decoded from brain implants, or when states deploy biometric surveillance to categorize citizens' worth, scientific innovation directly threatens human autonomy and privacy.",
