"Ultimately, science and human dignity are not adversaries when guided by democratic wisdom. By upholding universal human rights, fostering public scientific literacy, and ensuring that vulnerable populations share equitably in technological breakthroughs, humanity can harness innovation to elevate—rather than diminish—what makes us human."
