"Fortunately, language extinction is not inevitable. Successful revitalization initiatives—from Maori immersion schools in New Zealand to digital dictionaries, local radio broadcasts, and bilingual street signage—demonstrate that when governments grant official recognition and educational support, endangered languages can thrive alongside global languages."
