"However, philosophers, psychologists, and historians contend that treating culture as a superfluous ornament profoundly misunderstands human nature. From prehistoric cave paintings at Lascaux to songs composed inside wartime internment camps, human beings have consistently created art even under conditions of extreme material deprivation. Culture is the primary medium through which individuals process collective trauma, construct shared identity, and find existential meaning beyond mere biological survival.",
