    "texte": [
      "It is widely assumed that relocating to a foreign country automatically transforms a person into an open-minded, culturally perceptive citizen of the world. Stepping outside one's familiar environment undeniably exposes expatriates to unfamiliar social norms, languages, and historical narratives. When approached with genuine curiosity, navigating daily life abroad—from decoding indirect communication styles to adapting to different concepts of punctuality—can dismantle deep-seated stereotypes and cultivate profound empathy.",
