"Controlled 'correspondence tests'—in which researchers submit identical résumés or rental applications differing only in the applicant's ethnic-sounding name, gender, or disability status—consistently uncover persistent bias in hiring and housing markets. Often driven by unconscious stereotypes rather than overt hostility, implicit bias quietly denies qualified individuals equal access to career advancement and financial security.",
